claim.claim-text:
determine that bi-directional optical flow (BOOF) is enabled for a picture comprising a video block;
obtain a weight indication of bi-prediction with coding unit weights (BCW);
based on the weight indication of BCW,
determine to bypass BDOF for the video block, and
apply a weight to a reference prediction sample of the video block; and

obtain the first weight associated with the first reference picture based on the weight indication;
determine, based on the first weight associated with the first reference picture, a second weight associated with a second reference picture of the video block; and
apply the second weight to a second reference prediction sample associated with the second reference picture to generate a second weighted reference prediction sample, wherein the video block is decoded further based on the second weighted reference prediction sample.

determine that BCW is enabled for the first video block based on an indication in video data, wherein the weight indication of BCW associated with the first video block is obtained based on BCW being enabled for the first video block;
determine to perform BOOF for a second video block based at least in part on a second weight indication associated with the second video block;
determine a plurality of gradients based on a sample location in the second video block;
determine a motion refinement based on the plurality of the gradients; and
obtain a sample value associated with the second video block based on the determined motion refinement.

determine that weighted prediction (WP) is enabled for a second video block of a second picture;
obtain, in video data, a plurality of WP parameters associated with the second picture, wherein the plurality of WP parameters comprises a weight and an offset associated with the second picture, and wherein the plurality of WP parameters is associated with a global illuminance change of the second picture; and
obtain a sample value associated with the second video block using the weight and the offset associated with the second picture, wherein the second picture is decoded based on the sample value associated with the second video block.

